  "kind": "bit-matching-detail",
  "title": "AVEDEV computes the mean absolute deviation in plain binary64 arithmetic and returns #NUM! on zero numbers",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20430 and 20527, AVEDEV(number1, [number2], ...) coerces direct scalar arguments, ignores text, logicals, and blanks inside cell references or arrays while propagating errors, returns #NUM! when no numeric values are collected, and evaluates sum(|x - mean|) / n with binary64 sum/division. Matches 1,212/1,212 full-bank and 120/120 pinned AVEDEV rows.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across Excel 16.0 build 20430 (1,212/1,212 full-bank and 120/120 pinned AVEDEV rows in witnesses/AVEDEV.json) and Excel 16.0.20527.20088 in prefix_metadata (row 12, Data!A1:A3 = {1;5;3}).",
